   "source": [
    "# 18 HTTP STATUS CODES"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "90154ee3-4569-442b-a7fd-1a1c0fafe449",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "HTTP status codes are 3-digit codes sent by the server in\n",
    "the response to indicate the result of the client's request.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "HTTP/1.1 200 OK\n",
    "          ↑\n",
    "     Status Code\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "1xx → Informational\n",
    "      Request is being processed.\n",
    "\n",
    "2xx → Success\n",
    "      Request was successfully completed.\n",
    "\n",
    "3xx → Redirection\n",
    "      Further action is required.\n",
    "\n",
    "4xx → Client Error\n",
    "      Problem with the client's request.\n",
    "\n",
    "5xx → Server Error\n",
    "      Problem occurred on the server.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Common Status Codes:\n",
    "\n",
    "200 → OK / Success\n",
    "201 → Created\n",
    "301 → Moved Permanently\n",
    "302 → Found / Temporary Redirect\n",
    "400 → Bad Request\n",
    "401 → Unauthorized\n",
    "403 → Forbidden\n",
    "404 → Not Found\n",
    "500 → Internal Server Error\n",
    "503 → Service Unavailable\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "MEMORY TRICK:\n",
    "\n",
    "1xx → Information\n",
    "2xx → Success\n",
    "3xx → Redirect\n",
    "4xx → Client problem\n",
    "5xx → Server problem"
   ]
  }
 ],
